# Why this file is at the repository root when the project's documents are not.
#
# The owner deliberately moved the project's documents and configuration - README.md, pytest.ini,
# the requirements* files - into workspace/, and that preference is respected: nothing is moved
# back. This file is the one exception, for exactly the reason conftest.py is one: git applies a
# .gitignore only to the directory that holds it and below, so workspace/.gitignore cannot ignore
# config/local_config.yaml or wakeword-training/ up at the root - from there it ignores nothing at
# all. While this file was missing from the root the whole list below was inert, and `git status`
# offered 563 paths instead of 19: local_config.yaml and the owner's voice recordings among them,
# untracked but NOT ignored, one `git add -A` away from being committed. This is git tooling that
# has to sit at the root to do anything, not one of the documents the owner relocated. The copy in
# workspace/ is left exactly where they put it.

# V.O.I.D
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Local runtime state (tasks, checkpoints, logs) - never commit
.void/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.log

# Never commit secrets or local config overrides
config/local_config.yaml
.env
*.key
secrets.*
# ...except void/security/secrets.py: source code (a thin wrapper over the OS
# keyring; it holds no secret values). It is imported by config, the kill
# switch and the device gateway, so a clone without it cannot run.
!void/security/secrets.py

# Invoices name the owner's clients and what each was charged. `void invoice` writes the document to
# the working directory unless told otherwise, so the repository root is precisely where they land -
# invoice-VOID-2026-0001.pdf was sitting here, written by a test run.
invoice-*.pdf
invoice-*.md
invoice-*.txt
invoice-*.html

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Test run output
junit.xml

# The owner's voice recordings used to train and evaluate the wake word. These are personal
# biometric data and must never enter git history; the scripts and config beside them stay trackable.
wakeword-training/data/**/*.wav
wakeword-training/data/**/*.npy
# The rule above is anchored at data/, so it does NOT cover these two, and both must stay out of history:
#   personal_voice/ is the same recordings again (a staging copy of data/personal_positive) - personal biometric data;
#   backups/ is 1.1 GB of generated training snapshots (3 timestamped dataset+model copies), superseded and
#   referenced by nothing in the runtime or the training scripts.
# Both remain on disk; only Git ignores them.
wakeword-training/personal_voice/
wakeword-training/backups/
